{
  "_contract": [
    "Notes on the three blocks a real run shipped without. All three are OPTIONAL -- a plan that",
    "omits them passes every gate exactly as before -- so nothing warns you when they are absent.",
    "That is the whole reason they are written out here.",
    "trip.traveler_constraints -- what the traveller's body and diet require, carried from intake.",
    "dietary_or_religious_needs and mobility_notes are free text lists. allergy_severity is one of",
    "none | preference | intolerance | severe, and it is the difference between a dish the traveller",
    "would rather skip and one that ends the trip. allergy_card_text is the literal sentence handed",
    "to restaurant staff, in the local language. max_continuous_walking_minutes is a hard number the",
    "walking check reads: with it set, any single segment or activity that exceeds it fails the gate,",
    "and without it nothing measures the constraint the traveller actually stated.",
    "entry_context -- the entry conclusion, on the page. SKILL.md's own quality gate requires that",
    "the conclusion reach the page through this block, and this template, the skeleton and the HTML",
    "template all omitted it, so a real cross-border plan shipped with no entry section at all during",
    "reintroduced Schengen border checks. status is one of not_required | required_held |",
    "required_to_apply | unverified. traveler_basis is a status CATEGORY -- 'EU long-term residence",
    "permit holder' -- and never a document number or expiry date: it goes onto a page the traveller",
    "may share, and a category is what makes the conclusion rereadable a month later anyway.",
    "Delete the whole block when the trip never crosses a border; an unverified entry panel on a",
    "domestic trip is noise, and SKILL.md says not to raise entry as a blocker for a traveller",
    "staying home.",
    "days[].activities[].on_foot_minutes -- minutes of THIS activity spent on foot or standing,",
    "an integer >= 0. Segment walking_minutes covers only travel between stops, so a page can",
    "truthfully print '42 minutes on foot' for a day that schedules three and a half hours of it",
    "inside museums and markets. That happened, against a stated mobility limit, and the walking",
    "gate certified the number. Authoring it turns the second half of the day's walking on.",
    "",
    "intake_context -- REQUIRED, unlike the three blocks above. method is one of html_form |",
    "user_supplied | chat_fallback and each carries its own evidence: html_form names the intake",
    "file only the intake server writes; user_supplied says what the traveller supplied instead;",
    "chat_fallback carries declined_verbatim, the traveller's OWN WORDS declining the form, plus",
    "declined_at. It is required because the failure it guards is an omission: an assistant that",
    "skipped the form is the same assistant that would leave an optional key out, so an optional",
    "version would report clean on exactly the run that motivated it.",
    "",
    "attraction_tickets[].sale_opens_at -- REQUIRED on any ticket an activity actually schedules,",
    "and only those: a ticket listed as an option nobody put on a day cannot strand anyone. status is",
    "always_available | scheduled_release | at_the_door | sold_out_or_unavailable. opens_at is an ISO",
    "date-time and is required when status is scheduled_release. basis is one sentence saying where",
    "the rule came from -- it is the whole anti-rubber-stamp of this field, because someone who",
    "opened the official page can write it and someone who guessed 'always_available' cannot. A",
    "guessed value is a fabricated fact, which is worse than the blank this field replaces.",
    "Delete this _contract key before saving the real plan."
  ],
